The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (ret == -EAGAIN && !(req->flags & REQ_F_NOWAIT)) {
    if (io_arm_poll_handler(req)) {
        if (linked_timeout)
            io_queue_linked_timeout(linked_timeout);
        goto exit;
    }
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the queuing of linked timeouts is only executed if `io_arm_poll_handler(req)` returns true. If it returns false, the linked timeout is not queued, leading to a situation where linked timeouts are prepared but never processed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!io_arm_poll_handler(req)) {
    ret = io_prep_work_files(req);
    if (unlikely(ret))
        goto err;
    io_queue_async_work(req);
}
if (linked_timeout)
    io_queue_linked_timeout(linked_timeout);
```
Reason:
The fix ensures that linked timeouts are queued regardless of the result of `io_arm_poll_handler(req)`. By moving the queuing of linked timeouts outside the conditional check, it guarantees that they are always processed, thus resolving the issue of linked timeouts being left unqueued.

